            <ArticleTitle>Pd-Catalyzed one-pot sequential cross-coupling reactions of tetrabromothiophene.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>10289-10298</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c7ob02601c</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Unsymmetrical one-pot sequential cross-coupling reactions of sterically hindered tetrabromothiophene with arylboronic acid and an alkyne/alkene to afford selective bi-, tri-, and tetrasubstituted aryl/alkynyl-thiophenes with the aid of a palladium catalyst were described. The reaction proceeds via a site-selective Suzuki/Sonogashira coupling, followed by selective Sonogashira, Suzuki and Heck coupling reactions. This methodology has demonstrated an important framework for the synthesis of organic scaffolds.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
